ctr: black touch screen in the menu without bottom_menu.png

With bottom_menu.png the touch screen shows RetroArch's 3DS menu (resume,
save and load state) while the menu is open. Without it, 0002 left the
"Asset(s) not found" screen up for the whole session. Now the touch screen
stays black (and ignores touches) while the menu is open, and in game it
shows the idle picture (0004) or the usual "Tap the Touch Screen" text.

An injected title ships no bottom_menu.png: its pause menu is the top
screen only, like the Virtual Console's.

Applies on top of 0004, to RetroArch v1.22.2 (RETROARCH_REF in versions.env).

--- a/gfx/drivers/ctr_gfx.c
+++ b/gfx/drivers/ctr_gfx.c
@@ -84,7 +84,9 @@
 {
    CTR_BOTTOM_MENU_NOT_AVAILABLE = 0,
    CTR_BOTTOM_MENU_DEFAULT,
-   CTR_BOTTOM_MENU_SELECT
+   CTR_BOTTOM_MENU_SELECT,
+   /* The menu is open but there is no bottom_menu.png: nothing drawn. */
+   CTR_BOTTOM_MENU_BLANK
 } ctr_bottom_menu;
 
 typedef struct
@@ -1224,6 +1226,7 @@
